16.text:
May his name be eternal;
while the sun lasts, may his name endure; 
let peoples invoke his blessedness upon themselves;
let all nations count him happy.

21.text:
With pinions you will be covered;
you will find refuge under God’s wings—
whose fidelity is an encircling shield.

175.text:
Fair Babylon, you predator, 
a blessing on the one who repays you in kind
what you have inflicted on us;
